1"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022711/0001493152-26-022711-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-04-10","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226015971/0001493152-26-015971-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-03-31","form":"8-K","codes":["3.01"],"events":[{"label":"Delisting notice or listing-rule failure","kind":"listing","tone":"crit"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226014209/0001493152-26-014209-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-03-19","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226011614/0001493152-26-011614-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Snail, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Services-Prepackaged Software\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 3 years.","It reported $83.4m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 35.7% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 42.7%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($11.0m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 35.7% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $27.3m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 29.1% to 42.7% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $11.0m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Net cash of $9.0m against total assets of $56.8m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 65.0% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$14.2m) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1886894/000149315226022718/0001493152-26-022718-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022718"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 35.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.35,"consecutive":2